@namespace Glory2Him.WebApp.Components.CoreUI

@* Invites the reader to send in something of their own. Sits in a bordered, rounded panel so it
   reads as a call to action rather than another block of sidebar copy — the border is the theme's
   own, the same grey as the rules around it. The pencil is floated rather than set in a flex row,
   so it behaves like the article's dropcap: the body copy wraps around it and then back underneath,
   while the heading keeps the panel's full width. A little smaller than an author avatar, so it
   reads as an icon rather than a second portrait.
   Presentational only (ts-ui-001). *@

<div class="border rounded-3 p-3 p-lg-4 g2h-contribute @CssClass">
    <h4 class="mb-2">@Heading</h4>

    @* The pencil sits inside the paragraph, exactly as the article's dropcap does, so it floats
       against the body copy and leaves the heading on its own full-width line above. *@
    <p class="mb-3">
        <i class="bi @IconCssClass text-primary lh-1 g2h-contribute-icon"
           style="font-size:@(IconSizePx)px;" aria-hidden="true"></i>@Body
    </p>

    <a href="@Href" class="btn btn-sm btn-primary-soft mb-0">
        @LinkText<i class="bi bi-arrow-right ms-1"></i>
    </a>
</div>
